  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read",
      "items": [
        "Top row: baseline assessment to teacher-verifiable group evidence. Middle row: teacher material to source-backed draft and explicit review. Bottom row: follow-up assessment to persisted comparison.",
        "Arrows name the data carried. All browser inputs travel through FastAPI; PostgreSQL persists workflow records via backend adapters.",
        "Synthetic demo endpoints read versioned files from data/demo and use these same parsers, embedding, retrieval and comparison services. No seeded AI-output fallback exists."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Preserve evidence",
      "items": [
        "Preview validates and returns counts plus five sample responses; it does not persist. Analyze reparses the CSV, filters only grouping eligibility, and saves all normalized rows and detected groups.",
        "Group evidence preserves exact uploaded answers, student IDs, support and coherence. Correct and blank rows remain available in counts and persistence; outliers are not forced into groups.",
        "Material chunks retain exact normalized text and offsets in PostgreSQL. Retrieval returns text, chunk IDs and similarity; vectors are rebuilt from durable chunks after a restart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Gates and controlled failures",
      "items": [
        "Invalid files fail with structured errors. Too few eligible answers or no supported cluster returns insufficient_data.",
        "No passage meeting 0.42 returns insufficient_relevant_context; generation returns insufficient_context and saves no draft. Gemini failure or unknown citation also saves no draft.",
        "Generation validates the client-supplied retrieval packet and chunk IDs; it does not independently re-read and compare each passage before the provider call.",
        "Review saves edits while generated, or explicitly enters terminal approved/rejected state. Rejected or unreviewed intervention blocks results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Comparison and recovery",
      "items": [
        "Follow-up repeats validation and grouping; matching requires the same question and at least two baseline members in the chosen recurring follow-up group.",
        "No reliable follow-up match stores insufficient_data and omits improvement percentages. A match calculates prevalence, correctness and student transitions using transparent denominators.",
        "App localStorage saves workflow IDs; reload calls analysis/remediation/results GETs and reruns material retrieval. Durable records remain authoritative.",
        "Source evidence uses committed revision 5fb327f. Existing workspace UI, environment example and documentation changes are excluded from the pinned source claims."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
